===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hauss|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Germanic|hausaz|lang=is}}, cognate with Lithuanian {{term|kiaušė|kiáušė|lang=lt}}, Latvian {{term|kauss|kaûss|lang=lv}}; from the same basic Proto-Indo-European root as {{term|hodd|lang=is}}, {{term|hosa|lang=is}} and {{term|hús|lang=is}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/høyːs/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|øyːs|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|hauss|hausar}}

# [[skull]]
# {{context|anatomy|informal|or|slightly|derogatory|or of animals|lang=is}} [[head]]
# {{printing|lang=is}} [[header]] (text area at the top of a page)

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s1|h|au|s|i=?-}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|head}} {{l|is|höfuð}}, {{l|is|kollur}}

====Derived terms====
* [[fara á hausinn]] (to go bankrupt)
* [[fá í hausinn aftur|fá eitthvað í hausinn aftur]] (to have something boomerang on one, get something straight back)
* [[kýrhaus]]
* [[standa á haus]]
* [[þekkja hvorki haus né sporð]]
* [[þorskhaus]] (a cod's head; a blockhead)

